>> title: Ligurian Focaccia
>> servings: 12
>> cuisine: Italian
>> dish: focaccia
>> source: Samin Nosrat, Salt Fat Acid Heat; adapted from Diego with the help of Josey Baker
>> source: https://www.saltfatacidheat.com/fat/ligurian-focaccia
>> summary: A high-hydration, overnight focaccia with an olive-oil brine, from Salt Fat Acid Heat.

# Dough

:stir @{water|2 1/2 cups|600 g}, @{active dry yeast|1/2 tsp}, @{honey|2 1/2 tsp|15 g} in #{medium bowl} until dissolved => _yeast.
:whisk @{all-purpose flour|5 1/3 cups|800 g} with @{kosher salt|2 tbsp|18 g} in #{very large bowl} to combine => _flour.
:add _yeast and @{extra-virgin olive oil|1/4 cup|50 g} to _flour, stir with #{rubber spatula} until just incorporated => _dough.
:scrape #{very large bowl} clean and cover _dough with #{plastic wrap}.
:{rest|12-14 hours} _dough at room temperature until at least doubled.

# Pan and bake

:spread @{extra-virgin olive oil|2-3 tbsp} evenly on #{rimmed baking sheet|18x13 in} => _pan.
:release _dough from #{very large bowl} with #{rubber spatula}, folding onto itself gently, then pour onto _pan.
:pour @{extra-virgin olive oil|2 tbsp} over _dough and spread gently.
:stretch _dough to the edge of the pan with your hands underneath, pulling outward; repeat once or twice over 30 min as it shrinks.
:dimple _dough with the pads of your first three fingers at an angle.
:stir @{kosher salt|1 1/2 tsp|5 g} into @{water|1/3 cup|80 g} until dissolved => _brine.
:pour _brine over _dough to fill the dimples.
:{proof|45 min} _dough until light and bubbly.
:preheat #{oven|450F} with a rack in the center and #{baking stone} on it (or an inverted sheet pan), starting 30 minutes into the proof.
:sprinkle _dough with @{flaky salt|for finishing}.
:{bake|25-30 min} _dough on #{baking stone} until the bottom crust is crisp and golden, checked with #{metal spatula}.
:{bake|5-7 min} _dough on an upper rack until the top browns => _focaccia.
:brush _focaccia with @{extra-virgin olive oil|2-3 tbsp}; pooled oil absorbs as it sits.
:transfer _focaccia with #{metal spatula} to #{cooling rack} and cool for 5 min until easy to release, then cool completely.

# Serve and store

:serve _focaccia warm or at room temperature.
:store _focaccia wrapped in #parchment in an airtight container; toast or reheat before serving again, or freeze tightly wrapped.
